# SonoPlay v1.2.5

Released November 21, 2026.

## Playback and renderer reliability

- Albums keep playing through track changes, and the first track can start without restarting a few seconds later. SonoPlay checks that the renderer is playing the requested track. ([#24](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/24), [#32](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/32))
- Dragging the volume slider sends one volume command at a time. SonoPlay keeps the latest pending value and reports the requested volume while the receiver catches up. ([#26](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/26))
- An offline renderer is removed once, so its polling loop no longer interferes with playback on other renderers. ([#29](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/29))
- SOAP repair preserves literal ampersands inside XML CDATA and comments, including in stream URLs. ([#33](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/33))

## Troubleshooting

Set `LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` to collect more detail. `INFO` remains the default. Plex tokens are redacted, and routine access logs and repeated DLNA messages are quieter so failures are easier to find. ([#27](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/27), [#30](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/30), [#33](https://github.com/aquantumofdonuts/sonoplay/pull/33))

Thanks to [@kcgthb](https://github.com/kcgthb) for the reports, fixes, and regression tests behind this release.

## Upgrade

Existing configuration works as is. For Docker Compose installations using the published image, run:

```sh
docker compose pull
docker compose up -d
```

